---
// About.astro: Tech philosophy & background — no personal details
---

<section id="about" class="about-section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">about_me</h2>
    
    <div class="about-grid">
      <!-- Story Card -->
      <div class="terminal-card terminal-card-windowed story-card">
        <h3 class="card-heading"><span class="heading-accent">#</span> Background</h3>
        <p>
          I'm a senior backend engineer with ~6 years of experience engineering high-throughput backend 
          query engines, petabyte-scale data platforms, and autonomous agentic AI architectures across 
          NielsenIQ and TCS.
        </p>
        <p>
          At NielsenIQ, I scale the Discover platform query generation engine across millions of analytical 
          records with Java, Spring Boot, FreeMarker, and custom Snowflake UDFs, while building autonomous 
          AI operations agents and FastMCP-based incident triage systems. Previously at TCS, I achieved a 10x 
          performance speedup on proprietary in-memory database engines.
        </p>
        <p>
          Currently deep in the agentic AI space — building Google OKF-based knowledge engines, Model 
          Context Protocol (MCP) tool servers, OAuth 2.0 security proxies, and automated synthesis compilers.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Philosophy / Values -->
      <div class="terminal-card terminal-card-windowed philosophy-card">
        <h3 class="card-heading"><span class="heading-accent">#</span> Philosophy</h3>
        <ul class="value-list">
          <li>
            <div class="value-icon">⚡</div>
            <div>
              <strong>Systems Thinking</strong>
              <p>Every service is part of a larger system. I design for composability, failure tolerance, and observability from day one.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="value-icon">🔧</div>
            <div>
              <strong>Automate Everything</strong>
              <p>If a task is repetitive, it deserves a script. I build pipelines and tools that eliminate toil and free up human creativity.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="value-icon">🧠</div>
            <div>
              <strong>Ship & Iterate</strong>
              <p>Pragmatism over perfection. Get it working, get it tested, ship it — then refine. Speed and quality aren't opposites.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about-section {
    background: transparent;
  }

  .about-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .card-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .heading-accent {
    color: var(--neon-green);
    margin-right: 0.3rem;
  }

  .story-card p {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .story-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .value-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .value-list li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .value-icon {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    background: rgba(0, 255, 65, 0.08);
    width: 42px;
    height: 42px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-primary);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .value-list strong {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--neon-green);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }

  .value-list p {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .about-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
